---
export const prerender = true;
import '../styles/global.css';
import syne800 from '@fontsource/syne/files/syne-latin-800-normal.woff2?url';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy · 3DreamLab</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="How 3DreamLab Edge preview collects, uses, and protects personal data for sign-up, accounts, sessions, and project configuration."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://3dreamlab.com/privacy/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href={syne800} crossorigin />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="legal">
      <a class="legal__logo" href="/">3DREAMLAB</a>

      <div class="legal__inner">
        <h1 class="legal__title">PRIVACY<span class="accent">.</span></h1>
        <p class="legal__meta">LAST UPDATED 2026-10-19 · VERSION 1 · PREVIEW</p>

        <div class="legal__body">
          <p>
            This notice describes how we process personal data when you use the 3DreamLab Edge preview at
            edge.3dreamlab.com and related sign-up and account features on 3dreamlab.com.
          </p>

          <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
          <p>
            The data controller is a Finnish entity. For
            privacy requests, contact <a href="mailto:contact@3dreamlab.com">contact@3dreamlab.com</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>What we process and why</h2>
          <p>
            The following describes each category of personal data we process for the Edge preview. Your email (and,
            for projects, the origin URL) is needed to request and use the preview; without it we cannot approve or run
            your account.
          </p>

          <h3>Sign-up request</h3>
          <p>
            When you submit the form at /signup, we process your email, chosen tier, optional company name, optional
            project note, IP address, and the time of submission. We use this to decide on and answer your preview
            request. Legal basis: steps prior to entering into a contract at your request (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)); if you
            sign up on behalf of a company, our legitimate interest in handling that company's request (Art. 6(1)(f)).
          </p>

          <h3>Account</h3>
          <p>
            If you receive access, we process your email, an internal user id, and the time of account creation and
            last login. Legal basis: contract (Art. 6(1)(b)), or legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)) when you use the
            service on behalf of a company.
          </p>

          <h3>Login codes</h3>
          <p>
            We send 6-digit one-time codes by email. We store only a keyed hash (HMAC) of each code. Codes are valid
            for 5 minutes and are deleted after use or expiry. Legal basis: contract.
          </p>

          <h3>Session cookies</h3>
          <p>
            We use a strictly necessary HttpOnly cookie <code>app_session</code> containing a random session token; we
            store only a hash of it. Sessions last 30 days or until you log out; logging out ends all sessions. We also
            set a short-lived <code>login_id</code> cookie (10 minutes) that ties a login code to your browser. We do
            not use analytics or advertising cookies, so we do not show a cookie banner. Cloudflare Turnstile (below) may
            store a short-lived security token in your browser while you complete a form; this is strictly necessary
            to protect the forms from bots.
          </p>

          <h3>Security and abuse prevention</h3>
          <p>
            We process IP address and email in rate-limit and throttle records (for example failed codes and how many
            codes were sent). We keep these records for 30 days. Legal basis: legitimate interest in keeping the
            service and accounts secure (Art. 6(1)(f)).
          </p>

          <h3>Project data</h3>
          <p>
            In the console we process your project name, origin URL (your API base URL), cache rules, purge log, and
            usage counts (requests per day and cache hit/miss metrics). Legal basis: contract.
          </p>
          <p>
            The responses your API sends through the edge are cached on your behalf: for that content you are the
            controller and we act as your processor (see the <a href="/terms/">terms</a>). Cached copies expire under
            your rules and are purged when you delete the project.
          </p>

          <h3>Bot protection</h3>
          <p>
            Sign-up and login forms use Cloudflare Turnstile. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)).
          </p>

          <h3>Email</h3>
          <p>
            We send login codes, approval emails, and replies. Messages sent through the site contact form are used
            only to answer you and are kept until the inquiry and any follow-up are handled. Legal basis: steps prior to
            a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) or our legitimate interest in answering business inquiries (Art. 6(1)(f)).
          </p>

          <h2>Processors and transfers</h2>
          <p>
            We use processors: Cloudflare, Inc. (hosting, Workers, D1 database, edge cache, Turnstile; data may be
            processed globally on Cloudflare's network; the database is located in Western Europe) and Resend (email
            delivery; sending region EU, Ireland/eu-west-1; Resend keeps message content for about 30 days). Replies and
            contact messages are received in our business mailbox.
          </p>
          <p>
            Both providers are US companies, so data may be transferred outside the EEA. Cloudflare relies on its
            EU-US Data Privacy Framework certification and the EU Standard Contractual Clauses; Resend relies on the
            Standard Contractual Clauses in its data processing agreement. Ask us for details of these safeguards. We do not sell personal data and we do not use it for
            advertising.
          </p>

          <h2>Retention</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Login codes: until used or 5 minutes.</li>
            <li>Sessions: 30 days or until logout.</li>
            <li>Throttle records: 30 days.</li>
            <li>Rejected sign-up requests: 90 days, to handle repeat requests and abuse (legitimate interest, Art. 6(1)(f)).</li>
            <li>
              Account and project data: until you delete the account or project in the console (Settings), or 90 days
              after the preview ends.
            </li>
            <li>Invoices and accounting records for paid tiers: as required by the Finnish Accounting Act (up to 10 years).</li>
            <li>Backups and logs at our processors may persist for a short additional period.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection (including to
            legitimate-interest processing), and data portability. You can export your data as JSON in the console
            under Settings. We answer requests within one month.
          </p>
          <p>
            You may lodge a complaint with the Finnish supervisory authority: Office of the Data Protection Ombudsman
            (Tietosuojavaltuutetun toimisto), <a href="https://tietosuoja.fi">tietosuoja.fi</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>Automated decisions</h2>
          <p>We do not make decisions based solely on automated processing. Approval of preview requests is done by a person.</p>

          <h2>Children</h2>
          <p>The service is not intended for anyone under 16. It is aimed at business users.</p>

          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            We update this page and the “last updated” date. Material changes are emailed to account holders.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <footer class="legal__foot">
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
        <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <style>
      .legal {
        min-height: 100vh;
        min-height: 100dvh;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 4rem);
        padding: 1.25rem 5vw 2rem;
        background: var(--black);
        color: var(--white);
        overflow-x: hidden;
      }

      .legal__logo,
      .legal__meta,
      .legal__foot {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: var(--text-meta);
        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      }

      .legal__logo {
        align-self: flex-start;
        font-family: var(--font-heading);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: var(--text-nav);
        letter-spacing: 0.12em;
        padding: 0.9rem 0;
        margin: -0.9rem 0;
        color: var(--white);
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .legal__inner {
        max-width: 42rem;
        border-top: 2px solid var(--white);
        padding-top: 1.25rem;
      }

      .legal__meta {
        margin: 1rem 0 0;
        color: #b5b3ad;
      }

      .legal__title {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: var(--heading-lg);
        line-height: 1.05;
      }

      .legal__body {
        margin-top: 1.75rem;
        font-size: var(--text-body);
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: #b5b3ad;
      }

      .legal__body p {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
      }

      .legal__body h2 {
        margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
        padding-top: 1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
        font-family: var(--font-heading);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        line-height: 1.3;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--white);
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      }

      .legal__body h2:first-of-type {
        margin-top: 0;
      }

      .legal__body h3 {
        margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
        font-family: var(--font-heading);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        color: var(--white);
      }

      .legal__body ul {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
      }

      .legal__body li {
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
      }

      .legal__body a {
        color: var(--white);
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      }

      .legal__body code {
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.9em;
        color: var(--white);
      }

      .legal__logo:focus-visible,
      .legal__foot a:focus-visible,
      .legal__body a:focus-visible {
        outline: 2px solid var(--white);
        outline-offset: 3px;
      }

      .legal__foot {
        margin-top: auto;
        color: #9a9a9a;
      }

      .legal__foot a {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.75rem 0;
        margin: -0.75rem 0;
        color: #9a9a9a;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .legal__foot a:hover {
        color: var(--white);
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
